w: 1.Per-so-nent ho-di-e, Vo-ces pu-e-ru-lae, Lau-dan-tes ju-cun-de, Qui no-bis est na-tus, Sum-mo De-o da-tus. Et de vir-, vir-, vir-, Et de vir-gi-ne-o, Ven-tre pro-cre-a-tus.
w: 3.Cel-e-brate joy-ous-ly, Sound a loud ju-bi-lee, Prais-ing full mer-ri-ly, Him born new-ly for us, Join the an-gel cho-rus. Won-drous man-, man-, man-, Won-drous man-ner in this, How He comes be-fore us.
%verses 2 and 4 are printed too: 2. Omnes clericuli, Pariter pueri, Cantent ut angeli, Advenisti mundo, Laudes tibi fundo. Ideo, -o, -o, Ideo gloria, In excelsis Deo! 4. With your friends, cheerfully, Children come join the spree, Angels here sing with glee, Of the heavenly birth, oh, Letting all the earth know. Praise be-stow, -ow, -ow, Praise bestow, "Gloria, In excelsis Deo!" (Gloria in excelsis Deo = Glory to God in the highest)
%unsure pitches of lines 2 and 3 (low C in "Sum-mo De-o", "pro-cre-a-tus") read at normal crop, lines 2-3 not enlarged
%unsure lyric alignment by position only (several verses stacked on one staff, only verses 1 and 3 written as w:)
%bars hand-counted (2/2 = 8 eighths, 9 bars, no pickup)
